    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0158" n="788" xml:id="pg788"/>

                <head>No. 341.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_TB1"
                            type="from">Biddle</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30, 1872</date>.
                        (Received Dec. 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 89.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith a copy and translation of a constitution, dated the 9th of November
                    instant, framed by a National Constituent Congress, reforming that of the 16th
                    of October, 1871. The principal changes are the extension of the presidential
                    term to four years, without eligibility to re-election during a period of equal
                    length, and the enlargement of the executive authority in emergent cases.</p>
                <p>The leading principles embodied in the previous constitution are preserved, with
                    some changes in details, and that the secondary laws may conform thereto, the
                    President has decreed the re-assembling of the convention on the 15th day of
                    January, 1873, as per inclosure No. 2, to consider the laws of election; of the
                    state of siege; for the press; for procedures at law; and reforms in the civil
                    and criminal codes, and also in the laws, military and commercial.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_TB1">THOMAS BIDDLE</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d35-a1.xml" xpointer="d35-a1"/>
            </div>
